From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maago <maago@example.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:55:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Read posts under the policies
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

post_detail reads under visible too:

    -- policy: visible p
    ...
    WHERE p.id = :id AND visible(p)

and maago gen goes through. Every query that uses a policy now takes the
user, as the views do, between ctx and the database; nil is nobody:

    func PostList(ctx context.Context, u *auth.User, db maago.DB, p PostListParams) ([]PostSummary, error)

So ShowBoard and APIPosts take u *auth.User: a pointer, so anybody may
still ask. ExportBoard, a func(w, r), reads it from the request, as
DownloadAttachment does. The policies' :now joins each query's Params.

GetPost applies visible, as -- get: GetPost says, and takes the user and
the policy's now after the id:

    func GetPost(ctx context.Context, u *auth.User, db maago.DB, id int64, now time.Time) (Post, error)

A post u may not read is sql.ErrNoRows to it: not found, a 404. So
maySee goes, and so do the Hidden checks of Attach and editable: postPage
reads PostDetail alone, and DownloadAttachment is a 404 when GetPost is.
A hidden post is nobody's now, its author's and staff's neither: they no
longer publish, archive or delete it either.
mayChange stays: who may write is the views' to say, not a policy's.

What reads every post calls GetPostIgnoringPolicies(ctx, db, id): the
admin, and the tests that read back what they wrote.

The permission table shows what changed. A draft that bob, or ann, may
not change was a 403 to them, a page saying it is there; now it is not
there at all. Four rows, the drafts', where the 403s become 404s:

    post_publish     POST /posts/{draft}/publish        bob: 403 → 404
    post_publish     POST /posts/{old draft}/publish    bob, ann: 403 → 404
    api_post_publish POST /api/posts/{draft}/publish     bob: 403 → 404
    api_post_publish POST /api/posts/{old draft}/publish bob, ann: 403 → 404

The other rows keep their statuses: a published or archived post out
by its time is anybody's to read, and a 403 to change for whoever may not; a post to
publish later is its author's and staff's until then; a draft's files
and comments are its author's and staff's; the CSV and the lists show
what is out.

